Chris Waters from Netcom - Online Communication Services  (408 241-9760 guest)  writes:

>>you can #name that
>>category of lamp "oil lamp", and any lamp you find later that is not named
>>"oil lamp" is a magic lamp.
>
>Excuse me?  How do you name a category?  The #name command that I'm
>familiar with names a particular item, not a category of items.


When #name asks you if you want to name an individual object, hit 'n' --
it will name the class of objects instead.  A class-naming is distinguished
from an individual-naming so:  "a lamp called magic" is a class-naming,
"a lamp named magic" is an individual-naming.

